# Files that are executed by a Linux container must keep LF endings, whatever
# the checkout platform does. With core.autocrlf=true a Windows clone rewrites
# them to CRLF, Docker copies the working tree into the image, and /bin/sh fails
# on the trailing \r with an error that names a line rather than the cause.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# The vendored corpus is compared byte-for-byte between runs and its provenance
# is recorded per scan; line-ending rewriting would make identical fetches look
# like changes.
data/*.json text eol=lf
